.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLAB-PROM-TARGETS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm klab-prom-targets
.Nd write Prometheus's scrape targets from the machines and cluster running now
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
No configuration file here holds an address to scrape.
.Nm
finds them from what is running \(em virtual machine addresses through
.Xr kldload-vm-ip 8 ,
cluster nodes through
.Xr kubectl 1
\(em and writes one JSON file per kind of target in Prometheus's
.Ql file_sd
format, each replaced whole so Prometheus never reads half of one:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa klab-blue.json , Pa klab-green.json
The lab's blue and green machines, port 9100, labelled with site and
distribution.
.It Pa klab-kspawn.json
Machines made by
.Xr kspawn 8 ,
labelled with their cluster.
.It Pa klab-vms.json
Every other running machine.
.It Pa kubelet.json , Pa cilium-agent.json , Pa cilium-operator.json , Pa hubble-metrics.json , Pa tetragon.json
The cluster's nodes, on each component's metrics port.
.El
.Pp
A kind with nothing running gets
.Ql [] ,
so Prometheus does not complain of a missing file.
Prometheus rereads the files by itself.
.Pa klab-prom-targets.timer
runs it 30 seconds after boot and every 30 seconds after that.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the header comment and exit 0; any other argument is exit 2.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/prometheus/targets/
What it writes.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop with no machines running, on 2026-09-30:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cat /etc/prometheus/targets/klab-vms.json
[]
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
A running machine is an entry of the form
.Ql {"targets":["<address>:9100"],"labels":{"site":"vm","vm":"<name>"}} .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr klab 8 ,
.Xr klab-exporter 8 ,
.Xr kldload-vm-ip 8 ,
.Xr kspawn 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-20 five of the lab's machines were running and its target
file was empty: machines whose DHCP lease carried no host name were
dropped.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Names are written into the JSON as they are: a machine whose name holds
a double quote makes its file unreadable to Prometheus, and every target
in it is lost.
